  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conciliation Resources Core Support 2020-2024</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Conciliation Resources k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d 2020-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to improve peace processes and support peace initiatives, CRs Strategic Plan 2020  2025 aims at improving the effectiveness of peacebuilding and peace processes. CR&apos;s vision is to transform the way the world resolves violent conflict so that people work together to build peaceful and inclusive societies. The Strategic Plan sets out four goals:
1. Adaptive and alternative paths to peace: peacebuilding overcomes barriers to creating peaceful societies,&#xa0;
2. Connecting people and peace efforts: more coherent initiatives help prevent and reduce violent conflict,&#xa0;
3. Inclusion, gender and influence: excluded groups influence approaches to building peace,&#xa0;
4. People centered policy: international peacebuilding support puts people first.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sida&apos;s support to Conciliation Resources (hereafter CR) is a core support for 2020 - 2023, including an extension for 2024. Sida has been a core donor to Conciliation Resources since 2004. 

CR is an international non-governmental organisation (NGO) specialising in peacebuilding. Since its establishment in 1994, Conciliation Resources has been focusing on understanding conflicts, create linkages between the different groups involved, and ensure that people directly impacted by conflict take part in its resolution. CR works with over 70 partners in, for example, Georgia, Ethiopia, the Democratic Republic of Congo, Central African Republic,  Nigeria, Colombia, the Republic of Fiji, and Papua New Guinea. During the coming period CR&apos;s work is guided by their Strategic Plan &quot;Building better peace&quot; for 2020-2025. CR has a long-term and context specific approach in the contexts where they work which mean that the type of work varies between their various programmes. CR focus on connecting divided communities with a focus on inclusion of women, youth and other gorups in society. This is done at both the community level and in more or less formal peace process at a more political level, like in Ethiopia, Bougainville and Gerorgia-Abkhasia. In addition to the context specific work, CR is also doing more thematic work and comparative learning which is published in their publication series Accord. The organisation has built up these past years a special expertise in gender equality integration in peacebuilding and in the last few years the focus on the Youth, Peace and Security agenda has increased.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Sidas st&#xf6;d till Conciliation Resources (h&#xe4;refter CR) r&#xf6;r k&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r perioden 2020 - 2023 inklusive en f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning f&#xf6;r 2024. Sida har varit en k&#xe4;rngivare till CR sedan 2004. 

CR &#xe4;r en internationell icke-statlig organisation (NGO) som har specialiserat sig inom fredsbyggande. Sedan etableringen 1994 har CR fokuserat p&#xe5; att f&#xf6;rst&#xe5; konflikter, skapa kopplingar mellan de olika ber&#xf6;rda grupperna och se till att m&#xe4;nniskor som direkt p&#xe5;verkas av konflikter deltar i dess l&#xf6;sning. CR arbetar med &#xf6;ver 70 partners i till exempel Georgien, Etiopien, Demokratiska republiken Kongo, Centralafrikanska republiken, Nigeria, Colombia, Republiken Fiji och Papua Nya Guinea. Under den kommande perioden kommer CR:s arbete styras av den strategiska planen &quot;Att bygga b&#xe4;ttre fred&quot; f&#xf6;r 2020&#x2013;2025. CR har en l&#xe5;ngsiktig och kontextspecifik strategi i de sammanhang de arbetar i vilket inneb&#xe4;r att typen av arbete varierar mellan organisationens olika program. CR fokuserar p&#xe5; att skapa f&#xf6;rbindelser mellan splittrade samh&#xe4;llen med fokus p&#xe5; inkludering av kvinnor, ungdomar och andra grupper i samh&#xe4;llet. Detta g&#xf6;rs b&#xe5;de p&#xe5; lokal niv&#xe5; och i mer eller mindre formell fredsprocess p&#xe5; en mer politisk niv&#xe5;, som i Etiopien, Bougainville och Georgien-Abchazien. F&#xf6;rutom det sammanhangsspecifika arbetet g&#xf6;r CR ocks&#xe5; mer tematiskt arbete och j&#xe4;mf&#xf6;rande l&#xe4;rande som publiceras i deras publikationsserie Accord. Organisationen har de senaste &#xe5;ren byggt upp en speciell expertis inom j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering i fredsbyggande och under de senaste &#xe5;ren har fokuset p&#xe5; ungdomar, fred och s&#xe4;kerhetsagendan &#xf6;kat.</narrative>
  </description>
